# Accessibility (WCAG 2.1 AA)

**Canonical reference:** [documentation/client/standards/accessibility-standards.md](../../../documentation/client/standards/accessibility-standards.md).

## Must follow

- **Unified `label`:** In `packages/features/` and `apps/*/pages/`, use design-system `label` — not raw `aria-label`, `aria-labelledby`, or `accessibilityLabel` (`silverkey/no-direct-accessibility-props`).
- **Icon-only controls:** Every `IconButton` and icon-only `Button` must have a `label` (`silverkey/require-interactive-label`).
- **Modals:** Use `BaseModal`, `ConfirmationDialog`, or `AccessibleDialog`. No ad-hoc portaled overlays without dialog semantics and focus management.
- **Never** put `aria-hidden="true"` on focusable elements (backdrops, buttons).
- **Headings:** One `Title as="h1"` per screen; section hierarchy `h2` → `h3`.
- **Forms:** Use `Input` / `FormField`; errors use visible text + `role="alert"` (see `Input.web.tsx`).
- **Decorative icons:** Omit `label` on `Icon` (defaults hidden); meaningful icons get `label`.
- **Touch targets:** ≥44×44px — see [responsive-ui.mdc](./responsive-ui.mdc).

## React Native

- Use primitive `label` / `accessibilityRole` via `Box` and `Button` — same feature code as web where shared.
- Modals: `accessibilityViewIsModal={true}` on overlay; title → `accessibilityLabel`.

## After edits

Run `pnpm lint` and relevant a11y tests from `Client/`. See [ACCESSIBILITY_CHECKLIST.md](../../../documentation/client/qa/ACCESSIBILITY_CHECKLIST.md) for manual release checks.
